    \"<span class=sf-dump-key>identification</span>\" => \"<span class=sf-dump-str title=\"268 characters\">This is a very bright constellation, easy to find in the winter sky (December - March). It&#039;s located near the celestial equator, so you can see it from most places on Earth. It looks like a hunter, clearly marked by Orion&#039;s Belt (three bright stars in a straight line)</span>\"
